A **pool** keeps objects that are not in use and hands them out again instead of creating new ones. Unity ships one as `UnityEngine.Pool.ObjectPool<T>`; here is the idea in a few lines:

```csharp
public class Pool<T> where T : new()
{
    readonly Stack<T> free = new();
    public int Created { get; private set; }

    public T Get()
    {
        if (free.Count > 0) return free.Pop();
        Created++;
        return new T();
    }

    public void Release(T item) => free.Push(item);
}
```

`Get` reuses a free object if there is one and creates a new one only when the pool is empty. `Release` puts an object back. After a short warm-up, the game stops allocating bullets entirely.

